From 7f6d24d70918c9df897d726addf7970863718f89 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yangtse Su <yangtsesu@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 13:24:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(ffi): add rofd_document_get_page_size_mm
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Expose rofd-core's metadata-only page-size query through the C ABI, so consumers
that need every page's physical box — a document viewer filling its page-size
cache, for example — do not have to parse and cache each page's content.

The call returns the same value as rofd_page_get_size_mm for the same index. It
performs no content validation, collects no content warnings, and also succeeds
for a page whose content cannot be loaded.

- include/rofd.h: declare the entry point and its output transaction contract
- src/document.rs: implement it over Document::page_size via the shared boundary
- src/lib.rs: re-export the symbol
- tests/document.rs: value parity with the page handle, metadata-only behaviour on
  a page with an unresolvable font resource, and argument/index/alias rejection
- tests/c/expected-symbols.txt: extend the pinned export list
- README.md and the v1 design doc: record the new entry point

Verification:
- cargo fmt --all -- --check
- cargo clippy -p rofd-core -p rofd-render -p rofd-ffi --all-targets -- -D warnings
- cargo test -p rofd-ffi
- crates/rofd-ffi/tests/run_c_tests.sh
